This extension runs, as separate programs, software under other licences. Each ships with its own
licence files. It bundles no opentide and no Python: it runs the opentide the user installs (EUPL-1.2).

- The opentide engine (WASM), in dist/engine/ of every package: opentidehq/language-server's language
  server built for WebAssembly (opentide-wasm, from its opentide-wasm-web release zip), licensed under the
  EUPL-1.2. It ships with its LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.html (the Rust crates compiled
  into it), and the licences of the wasi-libc it links (dist/engine/licenses/). dist/engine/worker.js
  bundles its wasm-bindgen glue, from the same zip.
- The TextMate grammars in syntaxes/ other than opentide-config.tmLanguage.json are generated by
  opentidehq/language-server and copied from its release highlights zip; they are EUPL-1.2, see
  syntaxes/LICENSE.language-server and syntaxes/NOTICE.language-server.
- syntaxes/opentide-config.tmLanguage.json is copied from Even Better TOML (tamasfe/taplo) under the
  MIT License, see THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.

The package carries no runtime: it runs the opentide installed in the workspace (its `opentide`
command, else `python -m opentide`), or the one opentide.path names, else the engine (WASM) for editor
features.
